Line 3: This "[" starts a value inside the text, but there's no "]" to end it.
    say "Hello, [name".
                ^
End the value with "]", like "Hello, [name]!". To put a "[" in text, write it twice: "[[".

Line 5: This "]" doesn't end a value.
    say "a ] b".
           ^
To put a "]" in text, write it twice: "]]". A value in text goes between "[" and "]", like "Hello, [name]!".

Line 1: Something is missing after ",".
    say "Hello,", name, .
                      ^
Put the next piece after the comma, like "say "Hello,", name".

Line 4: There's no value between these brackets.
    say "Hello, []!".
                ^^
Put a value in them, like "[name]". To put a "[" in text, write it twice: "[[".

Line 6: I expected a value here, but found "]".
    say "[total plus]".
                    ^
A value is a number, some text in quotes, yes or no, nothing, or a name.

Line 7: I expected "]" to end the value in the text, but found "total".
    say "[total total]".
                ^^^^^
The brackets hold one value, like "[total plus 1]".
